 },
 "requested_at": "2026-11-13T20:08:24.597022Z",
 "text": "This clause is not enforceable. \n\nUnder section 20(1) of the *Residential Tenancies Act, 2006*, the landlord is statutorily responsible for providing and maintaining the rental unit in a good state of repair, fit for habitation, and in compliance with health, safety, housing, and maintenance standards. Section 20(2) explicitly provides that this obligation applies even if the tenant had knowledge of any state of non-repair before entering into the tenancy agreement. Because the landlord's maintenance duties under section 20 cannot be waived or transferred to the tenant by contract (as reinforced by sections 3(1) and 4(1), which render inconsistent provisions void), the clause has no legal effect.\n\nVerdict: not enforceable\nSection: 20",
